WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
I test a multi-region SaaS platform end to end.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
Parallel runs share one login and scarce SMS phone numbers.

00:10.000 --> 00:16.000
This is a public practice shop with synthetic data, not a work system.

00:16.000 --> 00:22.000
I search, filter, and check a cart total with a page object and a visible ready state.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000
Each run writes JUnit XML and an HTML report, then a dashboard.

00:28.000 --> 00:32.000
The dashboard shows the pass-rate trend, a daily chart, and run history.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
It separates flaky and real failures. Slack links to the run, published on S3 behind CloudFront.

00:36.000 --> 00:42.000
GitLab CI runs the suite on Kubernetes after deploy, nightly, and on demand.

00:42.000 --> 00:48.000
Jobs that share test data are serialized. Artifacts stay with the run, and an after-script no longer floods the log.

00:48.000 --> 00:54.000
Agent skills read the live UI through Chrome DevTools MCP, choose semantic locators, and scaffold the test.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
Review against team standards happens before merge. I am Beni Kun.
